  "schema": "catalog-conformance-supplement/1",
  "note": "2026-11-14 #2383 doors everywhere. Forty new immutable revisions, one per core building def (core-<name>@2; core-hall@3, after core-hall@2): make.args.doorThings leaves each outside ground-floor doorway bare, widened to at least 1.2 m, for a core/door@2 placed in it (templates, and door-fit/1 at boot in live worlds). Older revisions keep their bytes. A K=2 run of `conformance.mjs --k 2 --filter <ref>` for each new revision placed, baked, furnished and rendered every sample of all 40 defs. The findings (gallery-budget/triangles: 78, place/architecture: 2 pins) are gallery triangle budgets at large sizes and many floors, plus two layout findings from the generator's plans: core-lighthouse@2 at wallThickness.max (no entrance), the same as the pinned core-lighthouse@1, and core-prison@2 at random[0] (an unreachable cell), a kind pinned for core-prison@1 at other random samples. These are the same kinds already pinned for the @1 revisions (bsgen-20261021, z2-catalogue-20261020, known-20261015), and they are pinned here by the new hashes. No budgets, samples or gap checks were relaxed.",
